      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "\ndate = input()\nday1 = input()\n\n#parse the date\nd,m,y=date.split()\nleap = False if int(y)%4 or int(y)%100==0 else True\nmthdays = 30 if m[:3] in ['Sep','Apr','Jun','Nov'] else 28 if m[0]=='F' and not leap else 29 if m[0]=='F' else 31\n\n#find start day position\nstart = ['Monday','Tuesday','Wednesday','Thursday','Friday','Saturday','Sunday'].index(day1)\n\n#Fill calendar\ncaldays = [['  ' for i in range(7)] for j in range(6)]\nfor i in range(start, start+mthdays):\n    row, col = divmod(i,7)\n    day_num = f\"{i-start+1:02}\"\n    if day_num == f\"{int(d):02}\": caldays[row][col] = 'XX' #mark current day\n    else: caldays[row][col] = day_num\n\n#print top border\nprint('-'*22)\n#print month\nprint(f\"|{' '*((20-len(m))//2)}{m}{' '*((20-len(m))//2 + (1 if len(m)%2 else 0))}|\")\n#print year\nprint(f\"|{' '*8}{y}{' '*8}|\")\n#print empty line (with edge borders)\nprint(f\"|{' '*20}|\")\n#print days of week\nprint(\"|MO TU WE TH FR SA SU|\")\n#print separator line (dashes or underscores)\nprint(f\"|{'-'*20}|\")\n#print weeks of month\nfor i in caldays: print(f\"|{' '.join(i)}|\")\n#print bottom border\nprint('-'*22)\n",
